TerrainCraft engraving icon library
===================================

The icons in this directory come from four upstream sets and TerrainCraft's own
landmark drawings. `catalog.json` records, for every icon, which set it came from, and
for every set its version, license, license file and source; landmark icons also carry
their own license, credit line, sources and review state. `tools/build_icon_library.py`
regenerates this directory from the upstream npm packages and landmarks/manifest.json.

tabler/     Tabler Icons (outline style), a curated subset
            Copyright (c) 2020-2026 Paweł Kuna
            MIT License, full text in tabler/LICENSE
            https://tabler.io/icons

maki/       Maki, by Mapbox
            Dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0, full text in maki/LICENSE.txt
            https://labs.mapbox.com/maki-icons/

temaki/     Temaki, by the Rapid editor team, a curated subset
            Dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0, full text in temaki/LICENSE.md
            https://github.com/rapideditor/temaki

nps/        National Park Service map symbols (npmap-symbol-library)
            Symbols designed by the National Park Service. The repository is distributed
            under the BSD license in nps/LICENSE.txt (Copyright 2013, Mapbox, LLC), which
            must accompany redistributions.
            https://github.com/nationalparkservice/symbol-library

landmarks/  TerrainCraft landmark icons, dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0
            (landmarks/LICENSE.txt), except where landmarks/manifest.json says otherwise:
            - dem-ridgeline icons trace skylines from USGS 3DEP elevation data (public
              domain);
            - osm-footprint icons are drawn from OpenStreetMap building outlines and are
              produced works under the ODbL 1.0. Credit "© OpenStreetMap contributors"
              wherever they are used.

Changes: Tabler's invisible 24x24 bounding-box path and CSS class are removed; Maki's
and Temaki's XML declarations and element ids are removed; the NPS symbols' Illustrator
comments, ids, inline styles and fill colors are removed. Drawings are otherwise
unchanged.
